  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 21,
    "summary": "Do righteousness and justice—Follow after righteousness and mercy—Safety comes from the Lord.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "The king’s heart is in the hand of the Lord, as the rivers of water: he turneth it whithersoever he will.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "Prov. 8:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 19
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Every way of a man is right in his own eyes: but the Lord pondereth the hearts.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "Prov. 16:2."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "Prov. 24:12."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "Luke 16:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 21
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "To do justice and judgment is more acceptable to the Lord than sacrifice.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "1 Sam. 15:22."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "An high look, and a proud heart, and the plowing of the wicked, is sin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "OR Haughty eyes."
          },
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "2 Ne. 28:14."
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "OR the cultivating of wickedness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 36
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 66
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The thoughts of the diligent tend only to plenteousness; but of every one that is hasty only to want.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "TG Haste."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 33
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 81
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The getting of treasures by a lying tongue is a vanity tossed to and fro of them that seek death.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Treasure."
          },
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "TG Vanity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The robbery of the wicked shall destroy them; because they refuse to do judgment.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The way of man is froward and strange: but as for the pure, his work is right.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "OR Perverse is the way of a man of crime. Prov. 11:20."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 17
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 49
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 71
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "It is better to dwell in a corner of the housetop, than with a brawling woman in a wide house.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "IE than with a contentious wife as a companion."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "Prov. 19:13."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "Prov. 25:24."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The soul of the wicked desireth evil: his neighbour findeth no favour in his eyes.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "Prov. 3:29."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When the scorner is punished, the simple is made wise: and when the wise is instructed, he receiveth knowledge.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "Prov. 19:25."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The righteous man wisely considereth the house of the wicked: but God overthroweth the wicked for their wickedness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "2 Ne. 23:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 17
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 69
          },
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 103
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso stoppeth his ears at the cry of the poor, he also shall cry himself, but shall not be heard.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "Mosiah 4:16 (16–18)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A gift in secret pacifieth anger: and a reward in the bosom strong wrath.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "TG Anger."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "It is joy to the just to do judgment: but destruction shall be to the workers of iniquity.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "TG Injustice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 62
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The man that wandereth out of the way of understanding shall remain in the congregation of the dead.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Isa. 53:6; 2 Pet. 2:15 (12–15)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that loveth pleasure shall be a poor man: he that loveth wine and oil shall not be rich.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "TG Pleasure."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 90,
            "text": "TG Treasure."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The wicked shall be a ransom for the righteous, and the transgressor for the upright.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Isa. 43:3 (1–4)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 19
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "It is better to dwell in the wilderness, than with a contentious and an angry woman.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "Prov. 25:24."
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "Prov. 27:15 (15–16); 3 Ne. 11:29."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There is treasure to be desired and oil in the dwelling of the wise; but a foolish man spendeth it up.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "TG Treasure."
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "TG Waste."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that followeth after righteousness and mercy findeth life, righteousness, and honour.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "Matt. 6:33; 3 Ne. 12:6."
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "Prov. 8:35."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A wise man scaleth the city of the mighty, and casteth down the strength of the confidence thereof.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "Eccl. 7:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso keepeth his mouth and his tongue keepeth his soul from troubles.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "James 3:2."
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "TG Gossip."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Proud and haughty scorner is his name, who dealeth in proud wrath.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 9
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 28
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The desire of the slothful killeth him; for his hands refuse to labour.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Apathy; Laziness."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "TG Labor."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He coveteth greedily all the day long: but the righteous giveth and spareth not.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "TG Covet."
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "Prov. 3:27 (27–28); Luke 6:30; Eph. 4:28."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The sacrifice of the wicked is abomination: how much more, when he bringeth it with a wicked mind?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 63
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A false witness shall perish: but the man that heareth speaketh constantly.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A wicked man hardeneth his face: but as for the upright, he directeth his way.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "TG Hardheartedness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There is no wisdom nor understanding nor counsel against the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Understanding."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The horse is prepared against the day of battle: but safety is of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "Ps. 33:17."
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "OR victory."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 12
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 62
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
